      "notes": "Full batch (8): Sunday dinner for two, Monday dinner for two, and 4 lunch portions for the freezer with the farro. Cooked Sunday morning before breakfast with your mom. No Parmesan rind (Jami). Timeline, about 85 min with ~50 hands-on: 0:00 oven to 300°F; pat thighs dry, pepper only (no salt: 'salt and pepper' to season means none). Brown in two batches, skin-side down, in 1 tbsp oil in the Dutch oven, 5-6 min a side; plate them and DISCARD THE SKIN; pour off all but about 1 tbsp fat. 0:22 onion, mushrooms and 1/2 tsp kosher salt 6-8 min until browning; garlic and thyme 30 sec; flour 1 min; slowly whisk in the wine, scraping the fond; add broth and tomatoes, simmer, nestle the thighs, cover, oven 35-40 min to 195°F. 0:35 start the farro (20 min covered), then blanch the green beans. 1:20 thighs out, stir in sage. Freeze: cool, then pack 4 portions of 1 thigh + sauce with about 1 cup farro each, label and date, into the freezer within a day (keeps 2-3 months; lunch only). Thaw overnight in the fridge; microwave covered with a splash of water. Tonight: covered on the stove over medium-low 15-20 min (or 300°F oven 25 min) until 165°F. Salted light (1/2 tsp kosher in the whole pot): Jami, salt at the table.",
